    abstract = "The intertwining-branch auspicious floral pattern is one of the traditional Chinese patterns. It was widely used and representative of the decoration of blue and white porcelain during the Ming Dynasty, with rich cultural connotations and aesthetic values. However, at present, its application in the field of artistic and creative products is difficult to meet the aesthetic and functional requirements of modern society. AIGC technology brings new opportunities for the innovative design of traditional patterns. However, there is still a lack of systematic research and practice at present. The application of AIGC technology to innovate the intertwining-branch auspicious floral pattern can not only enhance the artistic value of intangible cultural heritage cultural and creative products, but also meet modern demands and promote the inheritance and development of traditional culture. This study aims to explore the application of AIGC technology in the innovative design of the intertwining-branch auspicious floral pattern, introduce its artistic creation process and steps, and verify the effectiveness and feasibility of this method through questionnaire survey methods, experimental analysis methods, etc.",
