    doi = "10.1145/3745133.3745189",
    abstract = "This paper explores the transformative role of integrated machines for large models in the field of artificial intelligence, particularly in addressing the challenges faced by enterprises in deploying these models. With the rapid advancement of generative AI technologies, large models have become central to AI infrastructure. However, issues such as technical implementation difficulties, privacy concerns, and high operational costs hinder their widespread adoption. Integrated machines for large models emerge as a solution, offering a synergistic optimization of hardware and software to transform complex AI technologies into user-friendly, plug-and-play tools. This study systematically reviews the key technologies and industrial trends of these integrated machines, providing insights into their potential to revolutionize enterprise AI applications across various sectors.",
    booktitle = "Proceedings of the 2025 International Conference on Digital Economy and Information Systems",
    pages = "334–339",
    numpages = "6",
