    doi = "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-443-33584-6.00018-9",
    url = "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B9780443335846000189",
    keywords = "3D printing in healthcare, AI digital twins, Autonomous AI, Blockchain, Blockchain technology, Cloud computing, Emerging trends of AI in healthcare, Innovations of AI in healthcare, Nanotechnology, Opportunities of AI in healthcare, Point of care, Point of care devices",
    abstract = "Artificial intelligence (AI) is leading the way in this revolutionary wave of emerging technologies that is changing the healthcare industry. With the goal of improving the healthcare industry by enabling customized methods to diagnosis, prognosis, and patient therapies, the field of artificial intelligence (AI) in medicine is expanding quickly across several medical specialties. The reader will learn about some of the most recent developments in artificial intelligence in this chapter, which begins with a discussion of some significant new trends in the field of healthcare AI. The chapter then goes on to cover the many advancements and prospects pertaining to AI technology in the healthcare industry. The benefits of AI technology for patient-centered care, remote patient monitoring, geriatric care, etc. will be covered in this chapter."
