    abstract = "Phenotypic screening using subclass B1 metallo-β-lactamase (MBL)-specific sulfamoyl heteroarylcarboxylic acid inhibitors (2,5-dimethyl-4-sulfamoylfuran-3-carboxylic acid and 2,5-diethyl-1-methyl-4-sulfamoylpyrrole-3-carboxylic acid) showed high sensitivity and specificity for detecting MBL-producing Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Acinetobacter spp. This practical and cost-effective method may support routine detection of MBLs in clinical laboratories lacking access to molecular diagnostic tools."
