    abstract = {With the rapid development of artificial intelligence (AI) technology and AI-generated content (AIGC), human-machine coordinated education endows college students with a new learning mode. In response to the pain points of college students, such as limitations in knowledge learning, academic emotional distress, weak innovation awareness, and insufficient problem-solving abilities, a new method that combines Extenics with the latest generation of AI technology is proposed. By analyzing the process, mechanism, variables, and implementation path of handling contradictory problems, a new paradigm for the intelligent handling of contradictory problems through the dual-helix integration of the human brain, information resources, and AI is constructed. This helps college students break through the bottlenecks of the knowledge explosion and lack of innovation and builds an intelligent "bridge" from big data to innovative solutions. It provides a new idea for cultivating and improving students’ problem-solving abilities.}
