    url = "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B9780323955041002076",
    keywords = "Lexical frequency, Word processing, Social media, Psycholinguistics, Frequency norms",
    abstract = "This article discusses lexical frequency norms, focusing on traditional and social media sources. Traditional norms were based on book corpora, while recent studies use subtitles and social media. Social media provides more spontaneous language data, enhancing predictions of word processing times. Combining multiple frequency sources, including social media, offers better predictions. Challenges include data privacy and the rise of bot-generated content. Adapting frequency norms to individual characteristics could improve prediction accuracy."
