    keywords = "Communication, Design, Meaning-making, MMSS, Mode, Modal resources, Multimodal social semiotics, Multimodal texts, Multimodality, Sign, Social semiotics",
    abstract = "Multimodal Social Semiotics (MMSS), as the conjunction of Social Semiotics and multimodality, forms a comprehensive theoretical framework for understanding communication across multiple modes (e.g. speech, writing, image, gesture) used in the making of multimodal texts in various social contexts. This article examines the development of MMSS as development as a theoretical, methodological, and interpretative framework—primarily associated with the work of Gunther Kress and Theo van Leeuwen—highlighting contributions from key scholars and identifying significant turning points. It traces the origins of MMSS, defines the key concepts and tenets of the theory, while offering a structured approach to operationalizing MMSS in research."
