    year = "2024",
    note = "The 11th International Conference on Applications and Techniques in Cyber Intelligence",
    issn = "1877-0509",
    doi = "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procs.2024.10.102",
    url = "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1877050924029028",
    keywords = "smart library, intelligent perception system, radio frequency identification, single shot Multibox detector",
    abstract = "RFID technology, as an important intelligent perception technology, provides a more efficient, convenient, and intelligent way for library management and services. However, the security issues of RFID (Radio Frequency Identification) systems have gradually emerged, such as tampering with RFID tags and system cracking. In order to address the security issues of RFID technology in smart libraries, a RFID security algorithm based on intelligent perception systems was studied. This algorithm utilized the location information, physical properties, and communication features of RFID tags to achieve location privacy protection, and improved the security of the algorithm by combining dynamic and static keys. The simulation results showed that the algorithm had a high recognition rate (Max: 94\%) and security (Max: 97.9\%), which can effectively achieve RFID system identification of tag identity, effectively prevent tag attacks and cracking, and improve system reliability."
}

