    doi = "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-323-95504-1.00167-8",
    url = "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B9780323955041001678",
    keywords = "Additional language development, Authenticity, Communicative language teaching, English language teaching, Essentialism, Existentialism, Foreign language teaching and learning, Language learning, Materials development, Multilingualism, Native-speakerism, Teaching English to speakers of other languages",
    abstract = "Authenticity is a well-trodden concept with enduring interest for academics across disciplines. This article offers a brief overview of the theoretical discussion of authenticity in language learning and teaching and reveals its points of connection with real-life practices. It discusses the definition and conceptualization of authenticity and explores the myths and dilemmas we face in facilitating learners' articulation and production of authenticity. This introduction lays the conceptual foundation for describing and understanding individual and collective choices and practices concerning authenticity across contexts of language education."
}

